--TEST--
`rule:enums/no-class-machinery` makes a case its own constant declared on the enum, so `Status::Live` under the cursor answers the case and leaves `enum Status` to the type request, `rule:ide/the-index-answers-the-cursor`
--FILE--
<?nvs
enum Status: int {
    case Draft = 1;
    case Live = 2;
}

$s = Status::Li<|>ve;
echo $s;
--REQUEST--
definition
--EXPECT--
case.nvs:4:10
